A binary indexed tree stores at each index k the sum of the last p(k) elements of the original array, where p(k)=k & ‑k. To obtain the prefix sum sum(1,k) the algorithm repeatedly adds tree[k] to an accumulator and moves to the preceding index k ← k ‑ p(k) (i.e., k -= k&‑k) until k = 0, visiting only O(log n) nodes【3】. The corresponding code is:

```c
int sum(int k) {
    int s = 0;
    while (k >= 1) {
        s += tree[k];
        k -= k & -k;
    }
    return s;
}
```【5】
